      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ganglion cyst of the longitudinal posterior ligament of the spine is a rare entity, only described in 11 cases. This lesion occurs in young subjects suffering from classical lombosciatica, and has perhaps a traumatic origin. Computerized tomography and MRI provide the diagnosis."},
